\**Note: If you have not finished {p:Rhapsodies of Vana'diel} and plan to very soon, you might consider finishing that before continuing.{br}**Once you start {M:The Warrior's Path|The Warrior's Path|The Warrior's Path}, your last chance to progress in Rhapsodies will be during {M:A Fate Decided|A Fate Decided|A Fate Decided}, after which you'll be unable to progress until the final cutscene of {p:Dawn}, which includes a Japanese Midnight wait.
=2 Walkthrough
* After your conversation with {p:Cid}, you will be off to fight 3 monsters all across the globe. They can be defeated in any order.

>***If you zone without checking the NM trigger for the cutscene after the fight, then the fight will reset and the NM must be fought again.**
=4 Boggelmann
* Travel to (E-7) in {z:Misareaux Coast} and check the Storage Compartment there to spawn a {p:Bugard} named {m:Boggelmann}.
** {p:Unity Warp} 122 will take you near it.
** It has high defense and uses {p:Blood Weapon}.
* Check the **Storage Compartment** again after it is defeated for a cutscene and obtain the {@k}{k:Vessel of light}.

!Misareaux Coast-map.jpg|right|Misareaux Coast map
=4 Cryptonberry Executor
* Head to {z:Carpenters' Landing} from the east entrance in {z:Jugner Forest} (J-8).
** {p:Survival Guide} to {z:Carpenters' Landing} is fastest.
** Alternatively the {p:Unity Warp} (Level 119) will bring you close.
** The {z:Abyssea - Vunkerl} maw is also nearby.
* Travel to (I-9) in {z:Carpenters' Landing} and look for a ??? near the water. Clicking this ??? spawns a {m:Cryptonberry Executor} (NIN).
** Shortly after he pops, 3 {m:Cryptonberry Assassins|Cryptonberry Assassin} (THF, SMN, BLM) will appear.
** They can all use their respective job's 2 hour ability. Avoid {p:Mijin Gakure} by killing the Executor first, and very quickly.
** {p:Astral Flow} is the next concern, but it is still significantly weaker then the Executor's {p:Mijin Gakure}.
** Make sure your party's HP remains high until the NIN and SMN are defeated.
* Check the ??? again once the Tonberries are dead to receive a cutscene.

!Carpenters Landing-map1.jpg|right|Carpenters Landing
=4 Dalham
* Travel to (F-6) in {p:Bibiki Bay} and look for a ??? inside a cave. Clicking this spawns a {p:Kraken-type|Category:Sea Monk} mob named {m:Dalham}.
** Both the {p:Survival Guide} and {p:Unity Warp} 119 are similarly close.
** It doesn't use any 2 hour ability although it may appear that it has been using {p:Hundred Fists} by the time the fight is over.
** The familiar "Dust Cloud" 2 hour animation can be seen at several points during the fight, however, they only indicate that {m:Dalham} is increasing its multiattack rate (roughly 1x 100-75%HP, 2x 75~50% HP, 3x 50-25% HP, 4x 25-0% HP), not using a 2 hour.
* Check the ??? after defeating {m:Dalham} for a cutscene.

!Bibiki Bay-map1.jpg|right|Bibiki Bay
=4 Finishing Up
* After all of the monsters have been defeated, return to {p:Cid} to obtain {@k}{k:Letters from Ulmia and Prishe}.
* Talk to Sueleen in the {z:Sealion's Den} (H-6) (near {z:Tavnazian Safehold} Home Point #2) for a cutscene.

